    "label": "cor:cmab",
    "number": "Corollary 6.6",
    "quote": "Consider stochastic full-bandit CMAB with $n\\ge2$, a general rank-$k$ matroid with $k\\ge1$, a nonnegative submodular mean reward, and Assumption~\\ref{ass:action-set}. Let $\\psi=O(nk^2\\log n)$ and $\\delta=8k$. Then for every horizon $T\\ge\\max\\{2,\\psi\\}$ there exist algorithms with $R_{1/e}(T)=\\widetilde O(n^{1/5}k^{4/5}T^{4/5})$ (non-monotone), $R_{1-1/e}(T)=\\widetilde O(n^{1/5}k^{4/5}T^{4/5})$ (monotone)."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Non-monotone case, 1/e-regret. Remark 3.5 gives an anytime version via doubling up to log factors."
